  "id": "auditory-space-perception",
  "term": "auditory space perception",
  "definition": "Auditory space perception is the perception of where a sound is located in space, understood mainly as judging its direction. In this historical source, it is described chiefly in terms of estimating the direction a sound comes from and comparing that judgment with the sound’s actual position.",
